From 51f4b60d4f837eee9b3998d81ed2ed53542045cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Sturla <rsturla@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Feb 2026 15:53:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add an OpenSSL backend for GHmac

For RHEL we want apps to use FIPS-certified crypto libraries,
and HMAC apparently counts as "keyed" and hence needs to
be validated.

Bug: https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1630260

This is a build-time option that backs the GHmac API with OpenSSL's
EVP_MAC interface. We dlopen libcrypto.so.3 instead of linking directly
so that GLib can still be built as a static library without depending on
a static build of OpenSSL.

We use the modern OpenSSL 3.x EVP_MAC API rather than the deprecated
HMAC_* functions.
---
 glib/gchecksum.c        |   9 +-
 glib/gchecksumprivate.h |  32 +++++
 glib/ghmac-openssl.c    | 312 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 glib/ghmac.c            |  16 +++
 glib/meson.build        |  12 +-
 meson.build             |   5 +
 meson.options           |   5 +
 7 files changed, 386 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 glib/gchecksumprivate.h
 create mode 100644 glib/ghmac-openssl.c

